window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_main-b107c3c818178f40"]={"key":"ny_main-b107c3c818178f40","group":"ny_main","uid":"b107c3c818178f40","rank":22,"title":"inglewood highmarsh transport coordination checklist","occupation":"office_admin_support_supervisors","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_main","prompt":"You are the First-Line Supervisor of Office and Administrative Support Workers at Inglewood Authority. By 18 September 2026, Hedda Abara needs a reusable checklist for Highmarsh Media to give Priya Bergqvist, whose single adult-social-care transport case in England has to be coordinated for a planned journey, a provider delay, and a same-day cancellation under rules and practice current to 1 September 2026. Produce one editable DOCX checklist that coordinating staff and Priya can use together. It needs to make clear what has to be obtained, who is responsible, when each action is due, what is communicated in each of the three situations, how confirmations are recorded, and what follow-up remains. Staff currently draw the line inconsistently between information that is essential before coordination can proceed and information that is useful but should not hold up a safe arrangement, so make that distinction operational without assuming that Priya knows social-care administration. The checklist also needs to enact and record the authorized change from telephone-only confirmations to documented confirmations, rather than merely mentioning that a change was approved. Keep the client-facing explanations short and practical: give enough context for Priya to know what she needs to do and when, but do not turn the document into a training manual, a general legal explainer, or a set of software click-through instructions. Include blank, reusable fields and a clear way to record incomplete, escalated, or not-applicable items without inventing facts. Keep the finished document to no more than three pages when printed, and write it so a coordinator can find the relevant path quickly during a live case. Save the completed file in the top level of the working directory where you start, using exactly the filename highmarsh_media_transport_coordination_checklist.docx.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `highmarsh_media_transport_coordination_checklist.docx` — An editable, reusable client transport coordination checklist for one adult social-care case in England, covering planned transport, provider delay, and same-day cancellation scenarios. (Use exactly the specified filename.; Place the file at the top level of the solver's starting working directory.; Keep the rendered document to no more than three pages.; Make the fields reusable and writable by coordinating staff and the client.; Do not include software click-through instructions or a general tutorial.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/highmarsh_media_transport_coordination_checklist.docx","bytes":45835,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/ad2c494cdd18c3fbaa9fce9699ebd8f8e7681c629f1ecdf3465088fd86c947fa.docx","sha256":"ad2c494cdd18c3fbaa9fce9699ebd8f8e7681c629f1ecdf3465088fd86c947fa","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Adult social-care transport coordination checklist\nReusable live-case form for the adult (including Priya) and coordinating staff\nScope: England | operating position current to 1 September 2026\nUse now: [ ] Planned   [ ] Provider delay   [ ] Same-day cancellation\nCurrent coordinator / last update: Name: __________  Date/time: __________\nAuthorised transition: telephone-only confirmations -> documented confirmations\nEffective date: ____________\nAuthorisation/source: ______________________\nChange owner: ________________\nFrom the effective date, record every material confirmation in the register. A telephone call may be used only when its material content and outcome are recorded at the time; a note saying 'called' is not a confirmation.\nMUST - before marked ARRANGED: adult/case match; exact journey; transport-relevant access and assistance; contact/consent arrangement; authority and limits; welfare action if no vehicle; and provider acceptance against all of these. Missing or contradictory? Mark [I], stop release, clarify or escalate; do not assume.\nSHOULD - record and pursue with an owner and due time, but do not delay a safe suitable arrangement: preferred driver or vehicle, usual route, optional reminder. A safety, access or support need is never a preference. Status key: [C] Complete [I] Incomplete [E] Escalated [N/A] Not applicable.\n1\nCase and journey essentials  |  Record only information needed to coordinate this journey\nAdult name / case or reference ID: Name: ________________________  ID: __________________\nAdult contact for journey updates: Number/address: __________________  Purpose: journey updates\nPreferred contact method, time and communication adjustment: ________________________________________________________\nAgreed representative / decision-support arrangement: Name/contact: __________________  Scope: __________________\nConsent to share transport details: [ ] Adult  [ ] authorised representative  [ ] other lawful basis; limits: __________\nEmergency or welfare contact / waiting plan: Contact: __________________  If delayed, unreachable or no vehicle: __________\nJourney date / required pickup / required arrival: Date: __________  Pickup: ______  Arrival: ______\nOrigin / destination: From: __________________________  To: __________________________\nReturn or onward journey: [ ] None  [ ] Return  [ ] Onward; timing/place: __________________\nAppointment / receiving contact / time-critical point: Contact: __________________  Effect of delay: __________________\nMobility, boarding, access, equipment or space: Transport-relevant detail only: __________________________________\nCommunication and reasonable adjustments: How to communicate / adjustment: ________________________________\nAssistance, escort or support needed: Who / what is needed: __________________________________________\nSecure record / provider need-to-know confirmed: Secure case record ref: __________  Provider told/confirmed: ______\nAuthority to arrange transport: Authorising person/source: __________________  Date/time: __________\nAuthority limits or conditions: Funding, journey, provider or other limit: _________________________\n2\nPlanned journey path  |  Complete in order; put material contacts in the confirmation register\nCheckpoint\nAction\nResponsible role / timing\nStatus and record\n1. Intake and authority\nCheck all MUST facts above, consent/contact arrangement and limits. If missing or contradictory: [I] stop, clarify or escalate; record exception.\nCoordinator + adult/ representative\nAt intake / before booking\nStatus: [ ]  Log no: ____\nIssue / named owner / due: __________________\n2. Suitable provider acceptance\nProvider confirms availability and ability to meet date, times, locations, access, equipment, assistance and escort needs. Capture provider and booking/reference before calling it arranged.\nCoordinator + provider\nBefore release\nProvider / ref: __________\nStatus: [ ]  Log no: ____\n3. Pre-journey / day-of readiness\nCheck expected arrival and adult readiness; no open MUST issue. Tell Priya/the adult the pickup window, where to wait, support arrangement and who to contact if plans change.\nCoordinator + provider + adult\nBefore departure / day of\nStatus: [ ]  Log no: ____\nExpected arrival: ______  named owner: ______\n4. Outcome and closure\nRecord actual pickup/arrival, or no-show/incident. List outstanding follow-up; do not close because a booking exists.\nCoordinator\nAfter outcome\nOutcome: __________________\nClosure owner / time: __________________\nLive routes for a change on the day\nUse the route that matches what has happened; keep the shared confirmation record current\nFor every material contact in either route, use the confirmation register on page 3: who/organisation, method, date/time, exact outcome or change, acknowledgement or inability to reach, outstanding point, next owner and due time.\nA\nProvider delay  |  Trigger: provider reports a delay or transport is not at the expected time\nDelay noticed/reported: Date/time: __________\nProvider/contact: __________________\nVerified revised ETA / obtained at: ETA: ______  time: ______\nProvider still meets access/support?: [ ] Yes  [ ] No  [ ] Unknown; detail: ______\nAction\nWhat to do\nResponsible role / timing\nStatus and documented record\nVerify the position\nAsk the provider for its current position, revised ETA and whether it can still meet recorded access, equipment, assistance and escort requirements. Do not promise an unverified ETA.\nCoordinator + provider\nImmediately\n[ ] C [ ] I [ ] E [ ] N/A\nLog no: ____\nNamed owner: ______\nAssess welfare and appointment impact\nCheck whether the adult is safe and able to wait, can be reached, and has the agreed waiting/welfare contact arrangement. Check impact on appointment or time-critical service.\nCoordinator + adult/ representative\nImmediately\nAdult reached: [ ] yes [ ] no\nDecision / welfare action: __________\nLog no: ____\nTell Priya/the adult and relevant parties\nUse agreed contact. Say: 'Your transport is delayed. The current verified estimate is __. Please __. We will update you by __.' Notify receiving service/welfare contact only as needed and authorised.\nCoordinator\nPromptly; after material change\nMethod/time/recipient/outcome\nin register, log no: ____\nNamed owner: ______\nContingency or escalation\nEscalate through the responsible welfare/escalation route when there is a safety or welfare concern, adult cannot be reached, a time-critical service may be missed, or provider cannot deliver required support. Consider wait, approved suitable alternative or rebook; do not promise one.\nCoordinator + escalation lead\nWithout delay if triggered\nTrigger / route / decision: __________\nLog no: ____  owner/due: ______\nReview and close\nVerify the actual outcome, communicate any material change, and leave follow-up/closure owner where unresolved.\nCoordinator\nAfter outcome\nOutcome: __________________\nClosure owner/time: __________\nB\nSame-day cancellation  |  Trigger: adult, representative, service or provider cancels on the journey day\nCancelled by / contact: _______________________\nDate/time / reason if known: Time: ______  reason: ______\nProvider dispatch status: [ ] not dispatched [ ] en route [ ] unknown; verify\nAdult's immediate transport need: [ ] remains [ ] does not remain [ ] unknown; action: ______\nAction\nWhat to do\nResponsible role / timing\nStatus and documented record\nVerify and capture\nRecord who cancelled, when, reason if known, dispatch status and whether an immediate transport need remains. Do not fill gaps with an assumption.\nCoordinator + caller/provider\nImmediately\n[ ] C [ ] I [ ] E [ ] N/A\nLog no: ____  owner: ______\nPrevent unnecessary dispatch\nTell provider to cancel/halt. Do not mark dispatch stopped until acknowledgement is documented; record inability to reach. Notify affected adult/representative, receiving service and welfare contact as needed.\nCoordinator + provider\nImmediately\nMethod/time/recipient/acknowledgement\nin register, log no: ____\nTell Priya/the adult\nSay: 'Today's transport has been cancelled. [Next step]. Please do not wait for a vehicle unless we confirm a new arrangement.' Record acknowledgement or inability to reach.\nCoordinator\nPromptly\nMethod/time/recipient/outcome\nin register, log no: ____\nNamed owner: ______\nReplacement or rebooking decision\nOnly arrange an alternative if the need remains and authority/limits, full journey/access/support requirements and provider acceptance are documented. A replacement is not automatic.\nCoordinator + authoriser + provider\nBefore any new arrangement\nDecision / booking ref: __________\nLog no: ____  owner/due: ______\nFollow-up and closure\nAgree next contact or rebooking action. Record unresolved welfare/service issue and who closes the record.\nCoordinator\nAfter decision/outcome\nNext action: __________________\nClosure owner/time: __________\nDocumented confirmation register and closure\nUse this shared record for planned journey, provider delay and same-day cancellation contacts\nTelephone is a permitted communication method only when the material content and outcome are recorded here at the time. Record every material planned, delay and cancellation confirmation; 'called' alone is not enough.\n3\nConfirmation register  |  Add rows if needed; write the exact decision or change\n# / scenario\nSubject\nPerson or organisation contacted\nMethod / date and time\nExact outcome or change\nAcknowledgement or unable to reach\nOutstanding point / next owner / due\n____\n[ ] Planned\n[ ] Delay\n[ ] Cancel\n________________\n________________\n____________________\n____________________\n________________\nDate/time: __________\n________________________\n________________________\n___________________\n___________________\nIssue: ______________\nOwner/due: __________\n____\n[ ] Planned\n[ ] Delay\n[ ] Cancel\n________________\n________________\n____________________\n____________________\n________________\nDate/time: __________\n________________________\n________________________\n___________________\n___________________\nIssue: ______________\nOwner/due: __________\n____\n[ ] Planned\n[ ] Delay\n[ ] Cancel\n________________\n________________\n____________________\n____________________\n________________\nDate/time: __________\n________________________\n________________________\n___________________\n___________________\nIssue: ______________\nOwner/due: __________\n____\n[ ] Planned\n[ ] Delay\n[ ] Cancel\n________________\n________________\n____________________\n____________________\n________________\nDate/time: __________\n________________________\n________________________\n___________________\n___________________\nIssue: ______________\nOwner/due: __________\n4\nIncomplete, escalated and follow-up items  |  Do not invent facts; name the owner and due time\nIssue\nStatus\nAction / escalation route\nOwner / due\nCompleted\nMissing or contradictory item / what is known\n[ ] I Incomplete\n[ ] E Escalated\n[ ] N/A\nClarify, action or responsible escalation route (not an assumption)\nNamed owner / due\nCompleted / date/time\n________________________________________\n[ ] I  [ ] E  [ ] N/A\n______________________________________________\n___________________\n___________________\n________________________________________\n[ ] I  [ ] E  [ ] N/A\n______________________________________________\n___________________\n___________________\nFOR PRIYA / THE ADULT\nPlease confirm your pickup point and time, the best way to contact you, and any help needed getting in/out or travelling. Tell us as soon as you can if plans change or you need to cancel. You can ask us to contact your agreed representative.\nSAFE RECORDING AND WELFARE\nRecord only information needed to coordinate this journey. Keep sensitive case information in the secure case record or channel; do not add diagnosis or unrelated clinical detail here. Record and escalate a safeguarding or welfare concern through the responsible local route. This checklist does not replace assessment, diagnosis or emergency response; use emergency response if there is immediate risk.\n5\nFinal disposition and closure  |  Check outstanding items before closing\nFinal position: [ ] completed  [ ] delay resolved  [ ] cancelled / no need  [ ] rebooked subject to confirmation  [ ] other\nActual outcome / incident or no-show: ______________________________________________________________\nOutstanding confirmation or follow-up: Log no(s): __________  action / named owner / due: __________________\nRecord closure: Closed by: __________________  Date/time: __________  [ ] outstanding items reviewed","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"T01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A DOCX file with the exact required filename is present.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Working-directory file listing.","grader_hint":"Confirm that the submitted top-level file is named exactly highmarsh_media_transport_coordination_checklist.docx."},{"rubric_item_id":"T02","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The deliverable contains editable text and writable fields rather than being only a flattened image or inaccessible scan.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"DOCX package contents and editable rendering.","grader_hint":"Open the DOCX and inspect its paragraphs, tables, or content controls; verify that a user can edit the instructions and fill the checklist fields."},{"rubric_item_id":"T03","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The rendered checklist is no longer than three pages.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered DOCX page count.","grader_hint":"Render with a standard offline office renderer and count pages, allowing normal default margins and fonts but not accepting unreadably tiny text as a workaround."},{"rubric_item_id":"T04","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies the England scope and states that its operating position is current to 1 September 2026.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope or document-control text.","grader_hint":"Look for both the England jurisdiction and the explicit 1 September 2026 as-of date, not merely the creation date."},{"rubric_item_id":"T05","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The template provides fields to identify the adult, case, and relevant contact details without requiring the user to place personal information in free text that has no defined purpose.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Case-information section and blank fields.","grader_hint":"Check that the reusable form can unambiguously link a person and a case to the transport record and has appropriate contact fields."},{"rubric_item_id":"T06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The journey record captures the date, required pickup and arrival times, origin, destination, and any return or onward journey relevant to coordination.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Journey-detail fields.","grader_hint":"Inspect the blank journey fields and verify that both timing and locations can be recorded precisely enough to coordinate a provider."},{"rubric_item_id":"T07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The checklist captures mobility, communication, accessibility, assistance, and escort or support requirements, with a place to record reasonable adjustments rather than leaving suitability to assumption.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Needs and accessibility fields.","grader_hint":"Look for transport-relevant access and support information, including how the provider will know about it and how an adjustment is recorded."},{"rubric_item_id":"T08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document distinguishes the adult's consent, communication preference, and any decision-support or representative arrangement from a generic assumption that the coordinator may share everything with anyone.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Consent, contact, or communication fields and instructions.","grader_hint":"Verify that the checklist records whether information may be shared for this coordination purpose and how Priya or an authorised representative should be contacted."},{"rubric_item_id":"T09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The template records an emergency or welfare contact and what should happen if the adult is delayed, cannot be reached, or is left without the expected transport.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Welfare and escalation fields.","grader_hint":"Check for both a contact/arrangement field and an actionable welfare response, not just a label saying 'emergency contact'."},{"rubric_item_id":"T10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The record identifies who authorised the arrangement and any relevant limits or conditions, so the coordinator does not silently extend the authority granted.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Authority or approval fields.","grader_hint":"Look for an authorising person or source, date or confirmation, and a way to note limits, rather than an unqualified 'approved' checkbox."},{"rubric_item_id":"T11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The checklist requires the coordinator to establish that the provider is available and able to meet the recorded journey and access requirements before treating the transport as arranged.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Provider-booking and suitability controls.","grader_hint":"Confirm that provider acceptance is tied to the actual date, times, locations, and support needs, rather than merely recording a provider name."},{"rubric_item_id":"T12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document draws an explicit and usable must-versus-should boundary, identifying which facts or confirmations are prerequisites and which useful details may be pursued on a best-efforts basis.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Priority labels, legend, or instructions used by the checklist.","grader_hint":"The distinction must affect action: a missing prerequisite should block, pause, or escalate coordination, while a missing nonessential item should have an owner and follow-up without automatically blocking a safe arrangement."},{"rubric_item_id":"T13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"When a prerequisite is missing or contradictory, the checklist tells the user to stop, clarify, or escalate rather than fill the gap with an assumption.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Exception handling and status instructions.","grader_hint":"Inspect incomplete-item guidance for a clear response, owner, and record of the issue; a generic 'check details' is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"T14","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The checklist gives at least one realistic example of a preference or convenience detail, such as a preferred driver or vehicle, that should be sought but does not hold up a safe, suitable arrangement when unavailable.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Must/should examples and related follow-up fields.","grader_hint":"Accept equivalent non-safety preferences, but verify that the document does not classify an accessibility or welfare need as optional merely because it is inconvenient to obtain."},{"rubric_item_id":"T15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each material action has an identifiable owner or responsible role, including actions shared with the client or provider.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Owner or responsibility columns/fields throughout the checklist.","grader_hint":"Sample actions in the general, delay, and cancellation paths and verify that responsibility is not left to an undifferentiated team."},{"rubric_item_id":"T16","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Timing is expressed against useful operational milestones, such as intake, booking, before departure, on the day, and after the outcome, with a due or completed time field.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Timing instructions and date/time fields.","grader_hint":"Credit timing that tells a coordinator when an action matters; a checklist containing only a single undated task list does not satisfy this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"T17","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The planned-journey path covers the progression from complete intake and suitable provider acceptance through pre-journey confirmation and readiness.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Planned-journey scenario controls.","grader_hint":"Verify that the planned path is more than a booking checkbox and includes the information and confirmation needed before the journey is released."},{"rubric_item_id":"T18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The planned-journey path includes a day-of or pre-departure check for the provider's expected arrival, the adult's readiness, and any unresolved prerequisite.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Pre-departure or day-of fields.","grader_hint":"Look for a usable checkpoint that can reveal a failure before the adult is left waiting, with a place to record the result."},{"rubric_item_id":"T19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The planned-journey path records the actual outcome, any incident or no-show, outstanding follow-up, and closure responsibility.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Outcome and closure fields in the planned path.","grader_hint":"A journey is not treated as complete solely because it was booked; verify outcome and unresolved-item capture."},{"rubric_item_id":"T20","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The provider-delay path identifies the delay as a separate trigger and directs the coordinator to obtain an updated position from the provider and assess its effect on the adult's welfare and appointment.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Provider-delay scenario section.","grader_hint":"Confirm that the delay route starts with verification and impact assessment rather than simply changing the ETA field."},{"rubric_item_id":"T21","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"For a delay, the checklist records the revised estimate, the time it was obtained, whether the provider can still meet the access requirements, and what contingency or escalation is needed.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Delay update, welfare, and escalation fields.","grader_hint":"Look for evidence that the revised ETA is verified and connected to a decision, not merely copied into a note."},{"rubric_item_id":"T22","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The delay path specifies timely, plain-language communication to Priya and other relevant parties, including what has changed and what action or waiting arrangement is expected.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Delay communication prompts and contact record.","grader_hint":"Credit only if the communication captures recipient, content or decision, and time/method; a bare 'notify client' is not enough."},{"rubric_item_id":"T23","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The delay path provides escalation triggers tied to safety, inability to contact the adult, a missed or time-critical appointment, or a provider unable to deliver the required support, without promising an outcome the coordinator cannot guarantee.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Delay escalation instructions.","grader_hint":"Check that escalation is conditional and practical, and that the checklist avoids presenting an unverified replacement or arrival time as certain."},{"rubric_item_id":"T24","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The same-day-cancellation path records who cancelled, when, why if known, whether the provider had been dispatched, and the status of the adult's immediate transport need.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Cancellation trigger and status fields.","grader_hint":"Verify that cancellation provenance and operational status can be reconstructed from the form."},{"rubric_item_id":"T25","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The cancellation path directs the coordinator to notify the provider and affected parties, with a recorded method, time, recipient, and acknowledgement or inability to reach them.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Cancellation communications and confirmation record.","grader_hint":"Look for a communication trail rather than an instruction that assumes notification succeeded."},{"rubric_item_id":"T26","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The cancellation path prevents an unnecessary dispatch and treats any replacement transport or change to the plan as subject to suitability, authority, and confirmation rather than an automatic promise.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Cancellation decision controls.","grader_hint":"Confirm that the document distinguishes stopping the cancelled journey from arranging a safe alternative when an ongoing need remains."},{"rubric_item_id":"T27","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"After a same-day cancellation, the checklist captures the agreed next contact or rebooking action, unresolved welfare or service issues, and who closes the record.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Cancellation follow-up and closure fields.","grader_hint":"A cancellation must result in a traceable next disposition, not simply a crossed-out booking."},{"rubric_item_id":"T28","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The confirmation record captures at least the confirmation subject, person or organisation contacted, method, date and time, exact outcome or change, outstanding point, and next owner.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Confirmation log or repeated confirmation fields.","grader_hint":"Inspect an empty record and determine whether another coordinator could reconstruct what was confirmed and what still needed action."},{"rubric_item_id":"T29","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document explicitly records the authorised transition from telephone-only confirmations to documented confirmations and includes an effective date, authorisation/source, and change owner.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Document-control or change-record text.","grader_hint":"Search for the telephone-only to documented-confirmations transition and verify that approval provenance and effective-date fields are present."},{"rubric_item_id":"T30","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The documented-confirmation requirement is applied consistently to planned, provider-delay, and same-day-cancellation communications, rather than appearing only in a front-page policy note.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scenario sections and their communication/logging prompts.","grader_hint":"Trace each scenario's confirmation step to a recordable method, time, participants, outcome, and follow-up."},{"rubric_item_id":"T31","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The checklist limits recorded information to what is needed for coordination, directs sensitive case information to an appropriate secure record or channel, and avoids inviting unnecessary clinical detail.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Data-handling prompts and field labels.","grader_hint":"Check both positive handling guidance and the absence of broad prompts for diagnoses or unrelated personal information."},{"rubric_item_id":"T32","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document gives a proportionate route for recording and escalating a safeguarding or welfare concern, while not presenting the transport checklist as a substitute for assessment, diagnosis, or emergency services.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Safeguarding, welfare, and scope language.","grader_hint":"Look for an instruction to record and escalate concerns through the responsible route, together with a clear limit on what this checklist establishes."},{"rubric_item_id":"T33","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Priya can understand what she is being asked to confirm or do without a social-care tutorial, while a coordinator still has enough operational context to use the form safely.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered document as a whole, especially labels, short explanations, and client prompts.","grader_hint":"Have a reviewer unfamiliar with this case inspect whether each client action is plain-language, specific, and bounded; penalise dense jargon, unexplained abbreviations, or tutorial-length exposition through failure to award this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"T34","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The completed artifact is practical as a reusable live-case control: the three scenario routes are easy to find, blank fields have enough room to write, statuses and exceptions are unambiguous, and the document does not depend on asking its author what an item means.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered DOCX and end-to-end walkthrough using a hypothetical case.","grader_hint":"Walk through one normal booking, one delay, and one cancellation using only the document; award credit only if the reviewer can identify the next action, owner, timing, communication, and closure record in each path without inventing missing conventions."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"This is a frontline administrative control document for a single adult social-care transport case, intended for shared use by a client with limited domain knowledge and coordinating staff. It must be concise enough for live use while preserving an auditable record of decisions, confirmations, exceptions, and follow-up.","difficulty_sources":["Draw an operational must-versus-should boundary for transport information and confirmations without being handed a rulebook.","Synthesize one reusable control document for planned, provider-delay, and same-day-cancellation situations.","Serve both a client with limited social-care administration knowledge and experienced coordinating staff without turning the checklist into a tutorial.","Enact and evidence a change from telephone-only confirmations to documented confirmations across every scenario."],"authoring_plan":{"reference_files":[],"gold_specification":{"artifact":"Create one editable DOCX reusable template, no more than three rendered pages, with blank fields and compact instructions. It should be case-neutral and suitable for one adult social-care transport case in England.","scope_and_control":["State the England scope and as-of date of 1 September 2026.","Include a document/change-control record showing the authorised transition from telephone-only confirmations to documented confirmations, with effective date, authorisation/source, and owner fields.","Do not invent local codes, names of teams, statutory thresholds, or software navigation conventions."],"general_case_controls":["Provide purposeful fields for adult and case identification, contact details, journey date, pickup and arrival times, origin, destination, return/onward journey, mobility and access requirements, communication preference, support or escort needs, consent/representative arrangements, emergency or welfare contact, and the authority or limits for arranging transport.","Require the coordinator to verify provider availability and ability to meet the recorded journey and access requirements before considering the arrangement ready.","Give every material action an owner and relative timing, with status, date/time, notes, escalation, and follow-up capacity.","Use explicit must/should or equivalent priority labels. Required items should be treated as blockers or escalation points when absent or contradictory. Useful preferences should be recorded and pursued without blocking a safe suitable arrangement; use a realistic example such as preferred driver or vehicle, while making clear that a safety or access need is not a preference."],"scenario_logic":{"planned":["Include intake completeness, authority and needs verification, suitable provider acceptance, pre-journey confirmation, and day-of readiness.","Capture actual outcome, no-show or incident, unresolved items, and closure owner."],"provider_delay":["Provide a distinct delay trigger.","Require provider contact and a recorded updated position, assess effect on welfare and the appointment, record revised ETA and suitability, communicate the change and expected action to Priya and relevant parties, and escalate when safety, inability to contact, time-critical service, or provider capability requires it.","Avoid promises based on an unverified ETA or unapproved alternative."],"same_day_cancellation":["Record who cancelled, time, reason if known, dispatch status, and whether the transport need remains.","Notify provider and affected parties with method, time, recipient, and acknowledgement/inability-to-reach fields.","Prevent unnecessary dispatch, and route any replacement or rebooking through suitability and authority checks rather than assuming it.","Record next contact/rebooking action, unresolved welfare or service issues, and closure."]},"confirmation_and_records":["Use a confirmation log or equivalent repeated fields containing subject, contacted person or organisation, method, date/time, exact outcome or change, outstanding item, next owner, and acknowledgement where relevant.","Make the new documented-confirmation practice apply in all three scenario paths. A telephone call may still be a communication method only when its material content and outcome are contemporaneously recorded; a note saying only 'called' is insufficient.","Provide a controlled way to mark incomplete, escalated, or not-applicable items without fabricating facts."],"safe_scope_and_audience":["Use plain language for Priya, explain only terms needed to act, and avoid a general social-care tutorial.","Include proportionate data minimisation and secure-record handling guidance; do not request unnecessary clinical or diagnostic detail.","Include a route to record and escalate safeguarding or welfare concerns and state that the checklist does not replace assessment, diagnosis, or emergency response.","Use accessible, dignified, person-centred transport language and preserve reasonable adjustments."],"derivation_and_review":"Build a blank, reusable gold from the above relationships rather than literal answer values. Verify offline by extracting DOCX text, rendering to PDF or images, checking the three-page cap, and walking through planned, delay, and cancellation cases. Confirm that a reviewer can identify action, owner, timing, communication, and follow-up without consulting any authoring notes."}},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"multi_artifact_bundle","structure":"supplied_template"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"transport_coordination_checklist","filename":"highmarsh_media_transport_coordination_checklist.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"An editable, reusable client transport coordination checklist for one adult social-care case in England, covering planned transport, provider delay, and same-day cancellation scenarios.","required":true,"constraints":["Use exactly the specified filename.","Place the file at the top level of the solver's starting working directory.","Keep the rendered document to no more than three pages.","Make the fields reusable and writable by coordinating staff and the client.","Do not include software click-through instructions or a general tutorial."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"plan_work","work_product":"form_or_template","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"office_admin_support_supervisors","sector":"healthcare_social_assistance","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":4.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"domain_expert","reviewer_policy":"Review the rendered DOCX as an England adult-social-care administrative control document. Check the content predicates from the editable text and tables, then conduct a live-use walkthrough for all three scenarios with a hypothetical single case. Confirm that the must/should distinction is operational, the confirmation change is recorded and applied, and the client-facing language remains concise.","minimum_reviewers":1,"known_limitations":["No reference files are supplied; the content is judged against occupational knowledge and generally applicable England social-care coordination practice as of the stated date.","Exact local escalation names and internal software fields are intentionally not prescribed, so equivalent professionally credible wording should receive credit."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:57:32+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:57:32+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:57:32+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:57:32+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_main/runs/b107c3c818178f40","declared_deliverables":["highmarsh_media_transport_coordination_checklist.docx"]};
